__pycache__/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.stage/
desktop.png

# What cargo builds. The device compiles its own; nothing built is kept here.
/target/

# The lint suite is a workspace of its own, so it builds into a target of its
# own, on a nightly of its own. Nothing built is kept here either.
/tools/explicit-rust/target/

# Where the sessions working on this tree keep their state, and where each of
# them puts a worktree of its own -- so this directory contains whole checkouts
# of this repository, one per session, each with a .claude of its own inside it.
# Nineteen gigabytes and fifty-six thousand files as this was written.
#
# Not ignored until now, which made `git add -A` in this checkout a command that
# tries to commit the repository into itself. Nothing had run it; that is the
# only reason it never happened.
.claude/

# The device this checkout talks to, set by direnv on entering the directory.
# An address is somebody's machine; the tree does not carry one.
.envrc
.direnv/

# What the sessions working on this checkout are told before they start: the
# commands, the shape of the crates, and the rules the code is written to.
#
# Not carried, because it is guidance for whoever is working on the machine
# rather than anything the desktop is made of. What this tree owes a reader is
# README.md and docs/, which argue in public and are held to it -- a second
# account of the same decisions, kept beside them and read by something else,
# is the arrangement where the two come to disagree and nobody finds out.
#
# It is also the only file here that would name the device by model. Everything
# published says what the machine is because the buttons are named for it;
# nothing published has to say it twice.
CLAUDE.md
